Render LaTeX math in cards with KaTeX

Purpose:
Show $...$ (inline) and $$...$$ (display) LaTeX math rendered in cards
of the desktop app. Upstream issue gingko/client#18.

Approach:
- Math.toElements (Elm) rewrites math in card content into
  <gw-math data-tex="..."> elements before marked renders it. Dollar
  rules follow pandoc's tex_math_dollars, so prices like "$5 and $10"
  stay text. Code spans, fenced code and \$ are left alone. The TeX is
  encoded as numeric entities so marked cannot mangle _ or *.
- The raw source stays inside the element as fallback text, shown
  where gw-math is undefined (web app).
- src/tauri/math.js defines gw-math, rendering with KaTeX on connect.
  This is safe with Elm's virtual DOM: elm-explorations/markdown is an
  opaque widget whose inside Elm never patches, and cards are lazy, so
  elements are only recreated when a card's content changes.
- esbuild-tauri.mjs copies katex.min.css and its fonts to tauri-web/.

Constraints:
- Stored content stays plain markdown; conversion happens only in
  rendering.
- Web app behaviour unchanged apart from the fallback text.
- Not rendered in breadcrumbs or the export preview.

